Package: fdmcorrect
Type: Package
Title: Sequencing-Error Correction of Deep Mutational Scanning Counts by False Double Mutants
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: person("Maximilian R.", "Stammnitz", email = "maximilian.stammnitz@crg.eu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Estimates the sequencing and PCR error rate of every single-nucleotide variant in a
    deep mutational scanning library from false double mutants, reads that carry a programmed
    multi-nucleotide codon variant together with a single-nucleotide change nearby, and subtracts
    the expected error reads from the variant counts. Rates are estimated with an empirical-Bayes
    Gamma-Poisson model with substitution-type and trinucleotide-context priors, pooled across
    libraries, with genuine double mutants removed from the evidence. Reads variant count tables
    in the format of 'dms_count'; used by the 'nf-core/deepmutscan' pipeline.
